{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A crushed reed.</b> It is called by the name of its end, and likewise ובגדי ערומים תפשיט (Job 22:6), and the meaning is he will not break a reed, and the meaning is he will not coerce:" "<b>And flax.</b> He will not extinguish it, for it is a slight thing, until it becomes dim, like והנה כהה הנגע (Leviticus 13:6). And there is a grammatical difference between them, for כהה of the Torah is a past-tense verb, while this כהה is an adjective of the noun. And the meaning is he will not harm a nation on account of his prophecy, but he will say what will truly come to pass:" "<b>For truth he will bring forth judgment.</b> Every nation, as it is destined to be by the decree of HaShem:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:31.191852657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}